1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

This Business Requirements Document (BRD) defines the complete business logic, domain rules, validation flows, pricing algorithms, event interactions, and UI requirements for an event‑driven modular monolith consisting of:

• Catalog Module (React + GraphQL)
• Inventory Module (Angular + REST)
• Orders Module (Angular + REST)

The system is designed for high modularity, event‑driven communication, domain isolation, and enterprise scalability.

2. SCOPE

This BRD covers:

• Business rules per module
• Cross‑module interactions
• Domain events
• Validation pipeline (Chain of Responsibility)
• Pricing engine (Strategy Pattern)
• UI/UX requirements
• Non‑functional requirements

3. PERSONAS

3.1 Customer
Interacts with product catalog, places orders, submits reviews.

3.2 Inventory Manager
Manages stock, quarantines, replenishments.

3.3 Catalog Manager
Creates products, updates metadata, handles quality issues.

3.4 Order Manager
Oversees order lifecycle, payments, shipping.

4. HIGH‑LEVEL ARCHITECTURE

Frontend Layer
• Catalog UI (React)
• Inventory UI (Angular)
• Orders UI (Angular)

Backend Layer
• Catalog Module
• Inventory Module
• Orders Module

Communication
• Asynchronous domain events
• No cross‑module queries

5. MODULE BUSINESS RULES

5.1 Catalog Module
• Owns product metadata
• Products cannot be deleted, only discontinued
• Quality issues trigger events
• CRITICAL issues mark product unsafe
• Reviews do not trigger events
• Updates propagate to Inventory

5.2 Inventory Module
• Owns stock levels
• Reservations are event‑driven
• Unsafe products cannot be reserved
• Quarantines triggered by quality issues
• Payment decrements stock
• Reservation is atomic

5.3 Orders Module
• Owns order lifecycle
• Order creation triggers reservation
• Payment allowed only if stock reserved
• Shipping allowed only if not recall‑risk
• Auto‑cancel if stock unavailable

6. CROSS‑MODULE RULES

Product Lifecycle
• Catalog → Inventory sync
• Discontinued → inactive in Inventory

Stock Reservation
• Orders → Inventory
• Inventory → reserved/not available

Quality Issues
• Catalog → Inventory quarantine
• Catalog → Orders recall‑risk

Payment
• Orders → Inventory stock decrement

7. DOMAIN EVENTS

Catalog
• ProductCreated
• ProductUpdated
• ProductDiscontinued
• ProductQualityIssueReported

Inventory
• StockReserved
• StockNotAvailable
• StockReleased
• StockDecremented
• StockReplenished
• StockQuarantined

Orders
• OrderCreated
• OrderPaid
• OrderCancelled
• OrderShipped
• OrderMarkedForRecall

8. VALIDATION PIPELINE (CHAIN OF RESPONSIBILITY)

8.1 Customer Validation
• Customer exists
• Active status
• Not blacklisted
• Valid billing info
• B2B VAT valid
• Credit limit sufficient

8.2 Stock Reservation Validation
• requested ≤ available
• Unsafe/discontinued → fail
• Auto‑cancel on failure

8.3 Payment Method Validation
• Card valid
• PayPal verified
• COD only B2C
• Invoice only B2B

8.4 Fraud Validation
• High‑risk country
• Failed payments
• High amount
• IP mismatch

8.5 Recall‑Risk Validation
• Active quality issues → recall‑risk
• CRITICAL → block shipping
• Quarantined → block payment

8.6 Business Rules Validation
• Max 50 items
• Max 30kg
• No alcohol weekends
• No electronics to PO boxes
• No COD > €500

9. PRICING ENGINE (STRATEGY PATTERN)

9.1 Standard Pricing
• Base price
• Tax
• Shipping
• Bulk discount

9.2 VIP Pricing
• 10–20% discount
• Free shipping
• Priority handling
• No stacking

9.3 B2B Pricing
• Wholesale price
• No VAT intra‑EU
• Invoice fee
• Contract shipping

9.4 Campaign Pricing
• Campaign discount
• Product discount
• Loyalty discount
• Supports B2G1, 50% second item, free shipping

9.5 Black Friday Pricing
• 30–70% discount
• Free shipping
• No returns
• No stacking

